@sfc-gh-truwase The reduction stream needs to wait for the default stream, which is easy to understand because the communication should not begin until the computation on that buffer is done. 

But should the default stream wait for the reduction stream? Yes, in case that the communication is longer than the computation. To make the overlapping safe, mutual wait between the two stream is needed. 

 The third figure in #5606 shows the logic I explained. But I haven't investigated further on the implementation that can fix this issue.

